pe":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Nozzle wear","items":[{"id":"Q05936","text":"Hardened Fortus 450mc head","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05937","text":"Hardened F900 head","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05938","text":"The T20F improves mechanical performance and is the recommended tip.","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q05939","text":"Annealing is a heat treatment process used to reduce internal stresses introduced during the FDM printing process.","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 11","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05940","text":"By heating the material to a controlled temperature below its melting point and holding it there for a set period, the polymer chains can relax and reorganize into a more stable, orderly structure.","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 11","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05941","text":"This change can improve certain physical and mechanical properties, such as tensile and flexural modulus, heat deflection temperature, and chemical resistance.","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 11","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q05942","text":"Samples were then annealed at 200 °C (392 °F) for three hours in a sand medium.","source":"R-STRATASYS-mds-fdm-antero-800na-0825a","at":"p. 11","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]}],"layers":[{"part":"tensileStrength","pairs":[],"unpaired":[{"id":"G098-06","name":"Stratasys Antero 800NA","why":"no flat value compared"}]},{"part":"tensileModulus","pairs":[],"unpaired":[{"i